.TH CTF-HUNTERD 1 "September 2026" "CTF Hunter 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctf-hunterd \- run the unprivileged CTF Hunter analysis daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctf-hunterd
.RB [ --database " PATH" ]
.RB [ --socket " PATH" ]
.RB [ --capture-socket " PATH" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctf-hunterd
collects explicitly configured file and terminal events, performs bounded flag
analysis, persists findings, and serves the versioned local IPC protocol. It is
designed to run as an unprivileged per-user systemd service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Set the SQLite database path.
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Set the per-user IPC socket path.
.TP
.BI --capture-socket " PATH"
Set the privileged capture helper socket path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctf-hunter (1),
.BR ctf-hunterctl (1),
.BR ctf-hunter-capture (1)
